Tue Nov 17 16:38:27 UTC 2026 - David Anes <david.anes@suse.com>

- Version bump to 1.2.7
  * An empty synonym field in a meaning line (a||b) no longer repeats the
    rest of the line as every later synonym. This affected the hu_HU, pt_BR
    and ru_RU thesauri
  * A line too long for the read buffer is cut short instead of split into
    extra lines
  * An index with no entry count line is rejected instead of loading with
    no entries
  * Open the .idx and .dat files in binary mode, so the index offsets are
    right on Windows
  * A meaning whose strings could not be allocated returns a count of 0
    with no synonyms and no definition
  * A word longer than any index word returns no meanings
  * Bound the index entry count by the size of the index file
  * Check the allocations and the path conversion in the Windows long-path
    open
  * example: fix the argument and line handling, and accept CRLF word lists
  * drop mythes-1.2.6-werror-sign-compare.patch (upstream commit 61597ef,
    inside tag v1.2.7)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov  5 19:18:50 UTC 2026 - David Anes <david.anes@suse.com>

- Version bump to 1.2.6
  * th_gen_idx.pl: add the -o option for the output path
  * Windows long-path support via _wfopen
  * Add the libFuzzer harness
  * Harden the .idx/.dat parsers: guard the truncated records,
    overflow check in the Lookup string sizing, clamp nmeanings at 8192
  * Add mythes-1.2.6-werror-sign-compare.patch (upstream 61597ef):
    the new guard in Lookup compares len with the int constant
    MAX_WD_LEN, so the build passes with -Werror=sign-compare
  * Mark COPYING as %license

